════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
 Stream lifecycle — when do substrates dry up?
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

 Each substrate has a finite, deterministic event list.
 After the last event tick, the runtime sees nothing
 further from the environment.

 substrate    events  last tick
 OQ#1            195 events, ticks 1..1924 (span 1924)
 long5k          453 events, ticks 1..4912 (span 4912)
 narrow_a         45 events, ticks 1..424 (span 424)
 OQ#2            164 events, ticks 1..4209 (span 4209)

 None of v2's canonical substrates are infinite.
 SyntheticStreamEnvironment takes Vec<(u64, Event)> by
 construction — once exhausted, no further events.

--- end ---
